    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. Here's a summary of what I changed to satisfy the specification.\n\n## What the spec required\n`householdId` must become deterministic \u2014 the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` \u2014 so owners with the same last name and postcode share it automatically. `sharesHousehold` should only *bypass the duplicate block*, not *create the link*. A second owner in the same household is a `409` unless it declares `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member and **not** flagged as a possible duplicate.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`Households.java`** \u2014 Now the single source of household identity. `id(...)` computes the 12-hex SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (dropped the old address-based key and `H-` prefix). Added `id(Owner)`, `id(OwnerFieldsDto)`, and `sameHousehold(a, b)` helpers. Removed the address normalization, `matches(...)`, and `resolveHouseholdId(...)` that the old opt-in link needed.\n\n**`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 Reduced to stamping the owner with its deterministic id (`owner.setHouseholdId(Households.id(owner))`). No more repository scan or stamping of existing members \u2014 the id is now self-derived, so same-household owners coincide automatically.\n\n**Duplicate block (renamed for the new meaning):**\n- Deleted `EnsureUniqueIdentity` / `DuplicateIdentityException` / its handler + escalation yml.\n- Added `EnsureUniqueHousehold` \u2014 rejects when an existing owner shares the request's computed household id, **unless** `sharesHousehold` is set. Backed by new `HouseholdDuplicateException` \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateExceptionHandler` (409) and its escalation yml. Wired the POST pipeline to the new step.\n\n**`DetectPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 A declared member (`sharesHousehold` true) is never flagged; otherwise it consults `PossibleDuplicates`.\n\n**`PossibleDuplicates.java`** \u2014 Now keys the soft match off `Households.sameHousehold` + differing telephone (was re-deriving last name/postcode itself).\n\n**`CountHouseholdMembers.java`** \u2014 Counts via `Households.sameHousehold`, so the household-size input to membership uses the computed id.\n\n**`IdentityKeys.java`** \u2014 Dropped the request-side overload (the old household-resolution path); the `identityKey` response field remains as a derived summary.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `householdId`, `identityKey`, `sharesHousehold`, and `possibleDuplicate` descriptions/examples to match.\n\nThe one acceptance test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) passes: same last name + postcode share an id (owner `b` uses `sharesHousehold` to bypass the 409), and a different last name yields a different id.",
